{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the problem and submitted the mitigation. The submission endpoint returned 200.\n\n**Root cause:** The `search` deployment's pod template had a stray label, `service-route: frontend`. The `frontend` service selects pods on that label, so it was sending about half of user traffic to the `search` pod, which doesn't serve the frontend on port 5000.\n\n**Fix:** I removed the label from the `search` deployment with `kubectl patch`. The `frontend` service now has only the real frontend pod as an endpoint. A test request to `/hotels` through the service returned hotel results.\n\nI didn't pull metrics or traces, so I haven't confirmed the latency effect. The `profile` pod restarted once at startup, probably because it came up before MongoDB was ready. It has been running since, and I left it alone."}}
